r, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:18px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'> &nbsp;</span></span></p><p><span style='font-size:18px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>We welcome any feedback on our data and dashboard so we can make future improvements, please fill out </span></span><a target='_blank' href='https://arcg.is/mT9qi0' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:18px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>our survey</span></span></a><span style='font-size:18px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'> with any comments or suggestions &nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><a target='_blank' href='https://arcg.is/mT9qi0' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:18px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'>https://arcg.is/mT9qi0</span></span></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style='font-size:14px;'><span style='border-color:rgb(192, 199, 202); box-sizing:border-box; line-height:1.25;'><strong>Squamish Now</strong></span></span><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:14px;'><span style='border-color:rgb(192, 199, 202); box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; line-height:1.25; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'> (SIM Now 2026) is a snapshot in time, consolidated of DOS (property and building permit information) and BC assessment datasets (Building Information Report &amp; Residential Inventory).</span></span></p><p><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:14px;'><span style='box-sizing:border-box; font-style:normal; font-variant-caps:normal; font-variant-ligatures:normal; font-weight:400; letter-spacing:normal; text-align:start; text-decoration-color:initial; text-decoration-style:initial; text-indent:0px; text-transform:none; word-spacing:0px;'><strong>Squamish Next</strong>&nbsp;(SIM Next 2026) presents a snapshot of future development, proposed through active land development applications submitted to the District of Squamish. This dataset is composed of DOS property and building permit informaation, in addition to incoming housing (#units) associated with&nbsp;Development Permits,&nbsp;Rezoning, and&nbsp;Official Community Plan applications. Projected housing units reflect five large neighbourhood developments (Waterfront, Oceanfront, Newport Ridge, Cheekeye and North Crumpit). These neighbourhood plans account for over 6,900 dwelling units supporting over 14,000 residents. If built, these developments are anticipated to be completed incrementally over 10-20 years.</span></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
